 "why": "The cosine series has insulated edges; h_side x perimeter x layer thickness / plan area is now added to the surface coefficient of each layer (Muzychka, Culham and Yovanovich 2003, eq. 29), in the steady sheet and the transient matrix; on a board with an outline the perimeter is that of the real outline (the model runs on the rectangle of the same area). The warning gives the sense of the error from the share of the edge heat put in the wrong place. Boards with h_side None (plate_uniform, plate_pad, one_layer_*) are bit-identical."
